==English==

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-prep phrase|[[on]] the [[spot]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} At that very moment; [[right away]].
#: ''He liked the house, so he made an offer '''on the spot'''.''
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} Having to [[answer]] or [[decide]] without [[warning]] or [[preparation]].
#: ''All the sudden questions put him '''on the spot''' and he had to think quickly.''
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} In a particular place.
#: ''This report comes from our man '''on the spot''' in Gaza.''
#: ''We exercised by jumping up and down '''on the spot'''.''
#* '''1928''', [[w:Dorothy L. Sayers|Dorothy L. Sayers]], "The Abominable History of the Man with Copper Fingers", in [[w:Lord Peter Views the Body|''Lord Peter Views the Body'']],
#*: I had accepted an engagement to go out with Mystofilms Ltd. in ''Fake of Dead Man's Bush''—the dwarf-men picture, you know, taken '''on the spot''' among the Australian bushmen.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|at that very moment}} (right) [[then and there]]
* {{sense|In a particular place}} [[in place]], on location, on site, on the premises, in the room

====See also====
* [[hit the spot]]
* [[on the dot]]
* [[on-the-spot]] (adj)

